      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We evaluated the safety and clinical usefulness of the same day protocol of exercise 99mTc-MIBI SPECT in 107 patients with heart diseases. No adverse event was observed except for one case of transient hypotension caused by the exercise. More than 95% of stress images and all of the rest images were judged as \"Excellent\" or \"Good\" in image quality. Overall sensitivity was 84.3% in detecting coronary artery disease, and no statistical difference was observed between the results obtained with Re-Ex and Ex-Re protocols. The examination was \"Quite Effective\" or \"Effective\" in diagnostic efficacy in 96.2% of the cases. We concluded that the same day protocol is a safe and useful method for diagnosing myocardial ischemia, which provides high image quality and valuable information."},
